+### Added
+
+- Cold-resumable read-only Coordination DAG (`"dag": true` on a declared-protocol `fgos coordination run` request): schema-version-3 sessions persist an immutable declaration, `show`/`chain` reconstruct derived node outcomes, and independent read-only operation nodes can overlap after predecessors settle. **Scope is read-only individual nodes only.** Mutating DAG nodes, per-node worktrees, mutation takeover, and fan-out-as-a-DAG-node remain deferred behind future evidence gates; a `dag: true` request that includes mutation or `fan-out` is refused before any session write. Compatibility: an older (schema 1/2) binary fails clearly with `schema-version-mismatch` on a schema-3 session and will not append to it; a current binary keeps legacy sequential semantics for schema-1/2 sessions and will not convert them to DAG mode on resume. How-to: `docs/how-to/run-a-coordination-session.md`; example: `docs/how-to/coordination-examples/dag-read-only-request.json`; proof: `docs/architect/agent-coordination/verification/cold-resumable-coordination-dag/`.
+
 ### Changed

 - `fgos-code-panel` / `fgos-plan-loop` driver skills now repeat Architecture Invariant 7 in the close template itself (never issue `cell-closed` while any node carries `sharedCwdCaveat` `status: 'recheck-required'`), document the two-request read-only DAG fan-out (including its expected shared-`--cwd` self-caveat), and name the refused-vs-pending resume rule plus two accepted `show`/`chain` projection gaps (`dag.counts.deferred` never reconstructed live; `nextAction` can say all nodes settled while a materialized node is still in flight).
